// Title: ESXi Syslog Configuration Change Via ESXCLI
// Sigma ID: 38eb1dbb-011f-40b1-a126-cf03a0210563
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Cedric Maurugeon
// Date: 2023-09-04 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, defense-impairment, T1685, T1690, T1059.012
// Description: Detects changes to the ESXi syslog configuration via "esxcli"
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrative activities
// References:
//   - https://support.solarwinds.com/SuccessCenter/s/article/Configure-ESXi-Syslog-to-LEM?language=en_US
//   - https://developer.broadcom.com/xapis/esxcli-command-reference/7.0.0/namespace/esxcli_system.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_esxcli_syslog_config_change.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/esxcli" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "system" and ProcessCommandLine contains "syslog" and ProcessCommandLine contains "config") and ProcessCommandLine contains " set"
